# Build context for apps/backend/api/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit prefers this file over the root .dockerignore when building with
# `-f apps/backend/api/Dockerfile`, and it replaces it rather than adding to it.
#
# The context is the repository root because the api is a workspace member, but
# only the api and the one library it imports belong in it. Everything else —
# both frontends, the ui-lib, the queue-coordinator, the Python workers — is
# excluded here, so touching them cannot invalidate a layer or slow the build.

# Deny everything, then re-open the paths the image needs. Intermediate
# directories are re-included explicitly: a directory that stays excluded is
# never walked, and nothing below it can be matched.
*

!/package.json
!/pnpm-lock.yaml
!/pnpm-workspace.yaml
!/.npmrc
!/tsconfig.base.json
!/tsconfig.backend.json

!/apps
/apps/*
!/apps/backend
/apps/backend/*
!/apps/backend/api

!/shared
/shared/*
!/shared/typescript-lib

# Never ship build output, host dependencies or secrets, whatever the rules above say.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
